    <div class="tg-hero__inner">
      <span class="tg-hero__type">Part IV of Five</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">The Answer Given: Church, Community, Mission, Message, and Works</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        The first three parts were largely diagnostic. This one turns from diagnosis to
        construction. Korah asked a question — <em>may I draw near?</em> — and the New
        Testament answers it, then builds an entire ecclesiology, mission, and ethic on the
        answer. The connection is not homiletical decoration: the specific vocabulary of
        Numbers 16 recurs in the New Testament at precisely the load-bearing points.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>See, here is water! What prevents me from being baptised?</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Acts 8:36">Acts 8:36</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
